  "character": "High-altitude, snow-sure, purpose-built. Europe's largest glacier for summer skiing. The no-nonsense freeride partner to Val d'Isere's polish.",
  "description": "Tignes sits at 2,100m in the Tarentaise valley, linked with Val d'Isere via the Espace Killy (300km). It has the largest glacier ski area in Europe (Grande Motte, 3,456m) for 11 months of summer skiing. Tignes is more purpose-built and less polished than Val d'Isere \u2014 less expensive, more functional, and with a passionate freeride and snowboarding culture. Hosted the 1992 Albertville speed-skiing events. Lively and young at heart.",
